---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="How to Use">
  <div class="pb-12">
    <header class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Get started</p>
      <h1 class="page-title mt-2">How to use Kalorec</h1>
      <p class="page-intro mt-3">Save recipes, plan a shop, and share the ones you choose.</p>
    </header>

    <ol role="list" class="mt-8 grid list-none gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <li class="surface-card p-5 sm:p-7">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-[var(--sage)] font-serif text-xl text-[var(--forest)]">1</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Set up your space</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="muted mt-4 leading-relaxed">Log in with GitHub, then choose a private repo for your recipes and shopping list. Create a private repo on GitHub first if you need one.</p>
        <a href="/settings" class="text-link mt-4 inline-block">Choose your recipe repo</a>
      </li>

      <li class="surface-card p-5 sm:p-7">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-[var(--sage)] font-serif text-xl text-[var(--forest)]">2</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Add a recipe</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="muted mt-4 leading-relaxed">Write one yourself or paste a recipe link to import it. Add tags and a photo from a file or HTTPS image URL.</p>
        <a href="/recipes/new" class="text-link mt-4 inline-block">Add a recipe</a>
      </li>

      <li class="surface-card p-5 sm:p-7">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-[var(--sage)] font-serif text-xl text-[var(--forest)]">3</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Make a shopping list</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="muted mt-4 leading-relaxed">Select recipes to add their ingredients. Quantities stay as written. Edit or check off items, then save your list. You can also copy or print it.</p>
        <a href="/shopping-list" class="text-link mt-4 inline-block">Open shopping list</a>
      </li>

      <li class="surface-card p-5 sm:p-7">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-[var(--sage)] font-serif text-xl text-[var(--forest)]">4</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Share when you want</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="muted mt-4 leading-relaxed">Choose a separate, empty public repo in Settings. Publish individual recipes, then copy your profile link to share them. You can add recipes from other public profiles to your own collection.</p>
        <a href="/settings" class="text-link mt-4 inline-block">Set up sharing</a>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <aside aria-labelledby="privacy-heading" class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--sage)] p-5 sm:p-7">
      <h2 id="privacy-heading" class="font-serif text-xl font-bold">Keep your private repo private</h2>
      <p class="muted mt-2 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">Saved recipes and shopping lists create Git commits, so older contents remain in your repo’s history. Unpublishing removes the current public recipe copy, but past public copies and Git history may still be accessible.</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Layout>
